.TH "DOCUMENTPICTUREINPICTURE.REQUESTWINDOW" "3JS" "April 25, 2026" "JavaScript" "JavaScript Reference Manual"
.SH NAME
DocumentPictureInPicture.requestWindow \- DocumentPictureInPicture:
requestWindow() method
.SH SYNOPSIS
\f[B]Secure context:\f[R] This feature is available only in secure
contexts (HTTPS).
.PP
The \f[B]\f[CB]requestWindow()\f[B]\f[R] method of the
\f[CR]DocumentPictureInPicture\f[R] interface opens the
Picture\-in\-Picture window for the current main browsing context.
It returns a \f[CR]Promise\f[R] that fulfills with a \f[CR]Window\f[R]
instance representing the browsing context inside the
Picture\-in\-Picture window.
.PP
The \f[CR]requestWindow()\f[R] method requires transient activation,
i.e., it must be invoked in response to a user action such as a mouse
click or button press.
.SH SYNTAX
.IP
.EX
requestWindow()
requestWindow(options)
.EE
.SS Parameters
.TP
\f[B]options\f[R] \f[I](optional)\f[R]
An options object containing the following properties:
.RS
.TP
\f[B]disallowReturnToOpener\f[R] \f[I](optional)\f[R]
A boolean value.
When set to \f[CR]true\f[R], this option hints to the browser that it
should not display a UI control that enables the user to return to the
originating tab and close the Picture\-in\-Picture window.
Defaults to \f[CR]false\f[R].
.RS
.PP
For example, in Chrome\(cqs implementation of this feature, the provided
UI control is a \(lqback to tab\(rq button in the Picture\-in\-Picture
window\(cqs top bar:
[IMAGE: browser window containing an embedded video player and multiple
control buttons, with a back to tab button in the top bar, highlighted
with a red box]
browser window containing an embedded video player and multiple control
buttons, with a back to tab button in the top bar, highlighted with a
red box
.RE
.TP
\f[B]height\f[R] \f[I](optional)\f[R]
A non\-negative number representing the height to set for the
Picture\-in\-Picture window\(cqs viewport, in pixels.
Defaults to \f[CR]0\f[R].
.TP
\f[B]preferInitialWindowPlacement\f[R] \f[I](optional)\f[R]
A boolean value, which defaults to \f[CR]false\f[R].
When set to \f[CR]true\f[R], it causes the Picture\-in\-Picture window
to always appear back at the position and size it initially opened at,
when it is closed and then reopened.
By contrast, if \f[CR]preferInitialWindowPlacement\f[R] is
\f[CR]false\f[R] the Picture\-in\-Picture window\(cqs size and position
will be remembered when closed and reopened \(em it will reopen at its
previous position and size, for example as set by the user.
.TP
\f[B]width\f[R] \f[I](optional)\f[R]
A non\-negative number representing the width to set for the
Picture\-in\-Picture window\(cqs viewport, in pixels.
Defaults to \f[CR]0\f[R].
.RE
.RS
.PP
\f[B]Note:\f[R] If one of \f[CR]height\f[R] or \f[CR]width\f[R] is
specified, the other one must be too, otherwise an error is thrown.
If both values are not specified, specified as 0, or set too large, the
browser will clamp or ignore the values as appropriate to provide a
reasonable user experience.
The clamped size will vary depending on implementation, display size,
and other factors.
.RE
.SS Return value
A \f[CR]Promise\f[R] that fulfills with a \f[CR]Window\f[R] object
instance representing the browsing context inside the
Picture\-in\-Picture window.
.SS Exceptions
.TP
\f[B]NotSupportedError\f[R] \f[B]DOMException\f[R]
Thrown if the API has been explicitly disabled (for example via browser
settings).
.TP
\f[B]NotAllowedError\f[R] \f[B]DOMException\f[R]
Thrown if:
.RS
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]requestWindow()\f[R] is not called from a top\-level
\f[CR]window\f[R] object.
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]requestWindow()\f[R] is called from the \f[CR]window\f[R] object
of the Picture\-in\-Picture window (i.e.,
\f[CR]DocumentPictureInPicture.window\f[R]).
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]requestWindow()\f[R] is called without transient activation.
.RE
.TP
\f[B]RangeError\f[R] \f[B]DOMException\f[R]
Thrown if only one of \f[CR]height\f[R] and \f[CR]width\f[R] are set, or
if \f[CR]height\f[R] and \f[CR]width\f[R] are set with negative values.
.SH EXAMPLES
.IP
.EX
\f[B]const\f[R] videoPlayer = document.getElementById(\(dqplayer\(dq);

\f[I]// \&...\f[R]

\f[I]// Open a Picture\-in\-Picture window with all options set\f[R]
\f[B]const\f[R] pipWindow = \f[B]await\f[R] window.documentPictureInPicture.requestWindow({
  width: videoPlayer.clientWidth,
  height: videoPlayer.clientHeight,
  disallowReturnToOpener: \f[B]true\f[R],
  preferInitialWindowPlacement: \f[B]true\f[R],
});

\f[I]// \&...\f[R]
.EE
